        "id": "d3822b1a6c4f4904b1115427ad452104-question-0",
        "ref": null,
        "question": "Does the same emptied-store condition arise with default snapshot configuration after a user restore on a monotonic log store, and does the node then keep re-creating snapshots at the restored index?",
        "source_ids": [
          "should_snapshot",
          "remove_old_logs",
          "restore_user_snap",
          "monotonic_scaffold"
        ],
        "hypothesis": "A node built over a monotonic log store that completes a user restore sets its last log, applied and snapshot indices to the restored index and then removes all logs, leaving the store's last index below the snapshot index, so shouldSnapshot returns true with no new entry and runSnapshots schedules another snapshot at that index.",
        "discriminator": "Build one real single-node cluster with the cluster helper's MonotonicLogs option and default TrailingLogs and SnapshotThreshold, apply a command, then complete a user Restore from an external snapshot whose index exceeds the current log. Record the log store's last index, the cached snapshot index, the applied index and shouldSnapshot immediately after the restore, and again after more than one SnapshotInterval has elapsed to see whether another snapshot at the same index was created. Control: the same cluster before the restore, where the store still holds the applied entries and the verdict must be false.",
        "disposition": null,
        "parent_id": null,
        "knowledge": null,
        "resume_conditions": null
      }
    ],
    "knowledge": [
      {
        "id": null,
        "ref": "@k_should_snapshot_underflow",
        "kind": "fact",
        "statement": "shouldSnapshot returns true whenever the log store's last index is below the cached last snapshot index, because the delta is computed as an unsigned subtraction and underflows; in that state the verdict does not depend on any new entry since the snapshot, and runSnapshots consequently calls takeSnapshot at the unchanged snapshot index. Observed operands (CheckRun 9cba2e79ff6c4019b0f0381690d9aaab): control store_last=4/snapshot_index=0 gives should_snapshot=false, and after the production snapshot path emptied the store, store_last=0/snapshot_index=4 with commit and applied index still 4 gives should_snapshot=true.",
        "conditions": "Node whose log store last index has fallen below the cached snapshot index, produced by the target's own compaction (for example a user snapshot with TrailingLogs=0) or by log removal; the FSM must still be able to answer Snapshot for the redundant attempt to produce a snapshot.",
        "source_ids": [
          "should_snapshot"
        ],
